fishing out his front door like he has  for the last 40 years  amerin niyomong lives in a community of  houses built on stilts  lining the edge of bangkok's busiest  canal  while the fishing might be convenient  the steady increase of commuter boats  rushing by  has become unbearable he says but  there's some relief  on the way a switch to electric boats  electric boats will generate less noise  and won't bother people so much  bangkok was once described as the venice  of the east  and many of the 10 million people here  still use its waterways to get around  and the boats used to carry them are  noisy big polluters putting toxins in  the water and into the air  so the city government has launched a  quieter and greener alternative a  three-month electric boat pilot program  right in the center of the capitol eight  boats to start and so far  they're carrying a thousand passengers a  day so while it takes four hours at the  pier to fully charge the batteries  to run the twin engines for the boat  these solar panels provide the power  for the instruments and the lights on  the vessel  the biggest challenge is changing  people's minds we have to encourage them  to switch from private vehicles to  public transportation  boats are a good option because of the  heavy street traffic so the introduction  of electric boats  can help both congestion and reduce  pollution the boats and most of the  components are manufactured  here in thailand only the motors and the  batteries are imported  there's hope that the indigenous  industry will expand so one day  the vessels will be 100 thai  i think ev is a kind of the initiate  the next step to encourage  people or even the government itself  to look more seriously think about  having the ev or electric vehicles  because  it is the next generation for  for the environmental friendly public  transportation  so while the government hopes that the  program is successful and that the  fossil fuel  powered boats are on the way out omran  could be getting some good news  his canal is set to be the next phase  for the electric boats  and that will allow him to fish in peace  and relative quiet  scott heidler al jazeera bangkok
 

